From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] ARM: exynos: Exynos5433 AUD trace bus out of the LPI
 handshake

As the vendor kernel does once at boot (pmu-exynos5433.c:472).  It did
not cure "Power domain AUD disable failed" alone, the next change does;
kept because the vendor kernel has it from boot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm/mach-exynos/suspend.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-exynos/suspend.c b/arch/arm/mach-exynos/suspend.c
index 41fee8c0f..426832307 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-exynos/suspend.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-exynos/suspend.c
@@ -1229,6 +1229,15 @@ static void __init exynos5433_pm_init(void)
 	if (!exynos5433_lpi_eagle)
 		goto err;
 
+	/*
+	 * Stock masks the AUD trace bus out of the low-power handshake once
+	 * at boot (pmu-exynos5433.c:472, exynos_eagle_asyncbridge_ignore_lpi).
+	 * Without it the AUD domain does not power off when exynos-lpass lets
+	 * it go in the noirq phase ("Power domain AUD disable failed") and
+	 * stays unreachable after resume (2026-11-05).
+	 */
+	exynos5433_ignore_aud_lpi();
+
 	pm_data = &exynos5433_pm_data;
 	exynos_pm_syscore.ops = pm_data->syscore_ops;
 	register_syscore(&exynos_pm_syscore);
-- 
